## Strongest exact claim

With `u=x+y^3`, the tame elementary automorphism `B9=(u,y+u^4)` has Jacobian `1`. Over `F_3`, `G9=A∘B9=(u-u^3,y+u^4)` is etale, of actual partial-`y` and total degrees `(9,12)`, with unit leading `y` faces `(-1,1)`, and is not injective. It is a source transform of the Artin–Schreier seed, not the conjugate `B9^{-1}∘A∘B9`.

The integer lift

```text
P = u - u^3 + 18 u y
Q = y + u^4 + 3 u^2 y + 18 y^2
```

satisfies, coefficientwise in `Z[x,y]`,

```text
det J(P,Q) = 1 - 81 u^4 + 54 y - 162 u^2 y + 648 y^2 ≡ 1 (mod 27),
```

keeps the same degree pair and unit faces, and reduces to `G9` modulo `3`. The W2 truncation has determinant `1-9u^4 ≡ 1 (mod 9)` and is not `1` modulo `27`. Omitting either `18`-term breaks the modulo-`27` gate. This is one explicit fixed-support determinant-one point over `Z/27` on the `(9,12)` checksum face.

## Sharpest non-claim

One finite-depth point over `Z/27`. Not a `Z/81` or all-depth tower, not a `Z_3` or characteristic-zero map, not a counterexample, not a maximum-twelve theorem, not TD6, not a classification of every lift of `G9`, not a group conjugate of `A`, and not a JC2 resolution.

